---
import ClubBase from '../../layouts/ClubBase.astro';
import MembershipForm from '../../components/club/MembershipForm.astro';
import { parseClub, parseLinks } from '@src/shared/club-content';
import club from '../../content/club.json';
import links from '../../content/links.json';

// `/membership/join/` — the club's own new-member application.
//
// ## ⚠️ This page is not linked from anywhere, and that is the state it ships in
//
// **Nothing stores an application yet.** `membership.membership_applications` does not exist:
// a table holding eighteen fields of personal data, including a date of birth and a home
// address, is a committee decision under this repository's own stop-and-ask rules, and it is
// not one an agent or a single volunteer takes. Two things are owed before the form can take
// a real submission:
//
//   1. **The committee's decision** on the table, with a retention period.
//   2. **Privacy-notice wording** for this collection and for passing a name, date of birth
//      and email address to England Athletics. `/privacy/` says nothing about either today,
//      and collecting an address under a notice that does not mention one is the breach
//      rather than the paperwork.
//
// So this address exists, renders, and is **reached only by typing it**: it is not in
// `CLUB_NAV`, there is no link to it from `/membership/`, and `tests/e2e/membership-join.spec.ts`
// asserts both absences. A form somebody can find and fill in that throws their answers away
// is worse than no form at all, which is the whole reason this is not wired up on a promise.
//
// **What is real here** is the markup, the eighteen rules it declares, the prices painted
// from the database, and the accessibility. What arrives with the table is the POST handler,
// the check-your-answers step, and the two emails.
//
// ## Every price on this page is read at request time
//
// ⚠️ **No figure appears in this file or in the component.** `worker/membership.ts` paints
// them from `membership.membership_types` on every request, so a fee rise is
//
// ```sql
// update membership.membership_types set price_pence = 500 where code = 'club';
// ```
//
// and no deploy — which is what the club asked for. The shipped text says the price is
// confirmed on the club's own form, and that is the honest answer when the database cannot be
// reached: a page that quotes a price somebody acts on had better be able to stand behind it.
//
// ## Nothing here is scripted
//
// The form is HTML and the browser's own constraint validation. Every test in this suite runs
// in a `no-javascript` project, and this page behaves identically there because there is
// nothing to degrade.

const meet = parseClub(club).meet;
const link = parseLinks(links);
---

<ClubBase
  title="Join Southville Running Club — new member application"
  description="Apply to join Southville Running Club. Annual membership, with the option of an England Athletics licence."
  canonical="https://new.southvillerunningclub.co.uk/membership/join/"
>
  <header class="club-phead">
    <div class="club-wrap club-wrap-narrow">
      <h1>Join Southville Running Club</h1>
      <p class="club-lede">
        Membership runs for a year. It supports the club, gets you into the members'
        WhatsApp community and local discounts, and — with an England Athletics licence —
        the affiliated rate at races.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="club-sec">
    <div class="club-wrap club-wrap-narrow">
      {
        /* ⚠️ **Said before the first box, not after the last.** What the club holds, who it
          goes to and how long it takes are the three things somebody wants to know before
          they start typing an address, and a notice under the submit button is a notice they
          read after they have already decided. The wording here describes only what the form
          does; the notice itself is owed — see this file's header. */
      }
      <div class="club-callout">
        <h2>Before you start</h2>
        <ul class="club-ticks">
          <li>
            It takes about five minutes, and you'll need your address and date of birth.
          </li>
          <li>
            You need to be <span data-membership-minimum-age>18</span> or over.
          </li>
          <li>
            We'll email you to confirm we've got your application. Nothing is charged here
            — the Membership Officer will be in touch about paying.
          </li>
          <li>
            You don't need to be a member to run with us. <a href="/run-with-us/">
              Come for a run
            </a> first if you'd rather.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <MembershipForm />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="club-sec club-sec-alt">
    <div class="club-wrap club-wrap-narrow">
      <h2>If you'd rather not fill this in</h2>
      {
        /* ⚠️ **`{' '}` before the link, and it is load-bearing.** Prettier reflows this
          paragraph so the newline lands between "or" and the `<a>`, and Astro compresses that
          newline to **nothing** — rendering "orask the Membership Officer". This repository
          has paid for the same trap three times already ("BristolBS3 1DB", "1DB.Map"), and it
          is invisible in the source every time. An explicit space survives the compression.

          ⚠️ **`meet.time` is the whole phrase**, "Meet 6.00pm for a 6.15pm start" — not a
          clock value — so it cannot follow "at". It is a sentence of its own here. */
      }
      <p>
        Come and find us at the {meet.venue} on {meet.days}. {meet.time}.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also{' '}
        <a href={link.committee.href}>ask the Membership Officer</a>{' '}
        through the committee page on our old site.
      </p>
      <p class="club-small">
        <a href="/membership/">What membership costs and what it includes</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ClubBase>
